WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.130
A visitor told our staff: the morning

2
00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:05.450
class does better than the afternoon

3
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.710
class, so we should end afternoon lessons.

4
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.890
The averages agreed.

5
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.360
But the averages were hiding something.

6
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:18.630
Today: how to read data claims carefully,

7
00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.310
and how to keep pupils' data private.

8
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.920
We looked inside the groups.

9
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.480
The afternoon class had most of the

10
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.960
pupils who joined this year, and many

11
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.100
were still learning English.

12
00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.780
Within each group, the two

13
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.480
classes scored about the same.

14
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.610
So the time of day was not the cause.

15
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.800
Two things can go together

16
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.540
without one causing the other.

17
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.560
Before you act on a pattern, ask:

18
00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.460
what else could explain it?

19
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.360
Be careful with small groups too.

20
00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.470
A class of eight can swing a lot

21
00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:54.990
from one test to the next.

22
00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.940
One good or bad day changes the average.

23
00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:01.910
Look at several tests before you judge.

24
00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:04.150
Now privacy.

25
00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.360
When I share results, I share the

26
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.140
class picture, not a child.

27
00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.980
Marks, health and family

28
00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.620
details stay private.

29
00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.130
A ranked list on the wall can

30
00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.890
hurt a pupil for years.

31
00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.750
Use pupil numbers instead of names.

32
00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:24.810
Collect only what your question needs.

33
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:28.340
Keep the list of names locked away, and

34
00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.020
delete the data when you are done.

35
00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:31.710
Quick check!

36
00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.160
Pupils who eat breakfast at

37
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.740
school get better marks.

38
00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.210
Does that prove breakfast

39
00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.550
causes better marks?

40
00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:41.720
Not on its own.

41
00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:43.750
Pupils who come early for

42
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.670
breakfast may also miss fewer

43
00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:47.910
lessons, or live closer to school.

44
00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:51.140
Breakfast may well help, but the

45
00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:52.880
pattern alone does not prove it.

46
00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:56.150
A fair test would compare similar pupils.

47
00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.910
In the app, open the bias lab.

48
00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.700
See how data that leaves out a group

49
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.520
gives unfair answers, and how fixing

50
00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:06.740
the data changes them.

51
00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:08.410
Your turn.

52
00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.320
You want to show parents how

53
00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.600
the class did in a test.

54
00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.270
What is the safest thing to share?

55
00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:18.270
The class average and spread, not names.

56
00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.750
Remember: look inside the groups, ask

57
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.030
what else could explain a pattern, and

58
00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:25.910
be careful with small groups.

59
00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.760
Share the class, never the child.

60
00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.260
Try it in class tomorrow: bring one

61
00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:34.420
claim from a newspaper or a poster.

62
00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.550
Ask your pupils what else could explain

63
00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.690
it, and what data would check it.
